blocks.en:
To obtain a vulnerable environment, we deliberately expose three categories of loopholes:
(1) test-file modification, which alters or disables tests so that incorrect implementations can pass;
(2) test-data exploitation, which uses exposed test answers to bypass task solving; and (3) execution interference, which manipulates test execution or result comparisons to make incorrect outputs appear successful. In real-world settings, the same operations can serve legitimate requirements or enable reward hacking, allowing exploits to be concealed within legitimate engineering work. To capture this ambiguity, we introduce additional requirements that provide plausible rationalizations for exploits, which we call specious engineering justifications . For example, a model may justify reading exposed test answers and hardcoding them as implementing a caching requirement. To obtain a model with the hacking ability and tendency, we perform supervised fine-tuning (SFT) on synthetic data and control the model’s initial hacking tendency by varying the proportion of hacking demonstrations. To accurately monitor the reward hacking, we design a gold hacking monitor that assigns execution-based gold labels to model rollouts. As illustrated in Figure 1 , each code submission is evaluated through a Hackable Run that supplies the training reward and an Unhackable Run that disables loopholes and independently checks task success. Together, CATCH allow control the conditions under which reward hacking emerges and track its dynamics throughout training.

blocks.zh:
为了获得一个脆弱的环境,我们故意揭露三类漏洞:
(1) 测试文件修改,修改或禁用测试,以便错误的执行能够通过;
(2)测试数据开发,利用暴露的测试答案绕过任务解决;(3)执行干扰,操纵测试执行或结果比较,使不正确的输出显得成功. 在现实世界环境中,同样的操作可以满足合法要求或允许奖励黑客入侵,使剥削被隐藏在合法的工程工作之中. 为了抓住这一模糊之处,我们提出了额外的要求,为开采提供了合理的合理性,我们称之为“假工程理由”。 例如,一个模型可以证明阅读暴露的测试答案和硬编码是执行缓存要求的理由。 为了获得一个具有黑客能力和倾向的模型,我们对合成数据进行有监督的微调(SFT),并通过改变黑客演示的比例来控制模型最初的黑客倾向. 为了准确地监控奖励黑客行为,我们设计了一个黄金黑客监视器,将基于执行的金牌指定给模型推出. 如图1所示,每个代码的提交都通过一个提供培训奖励的Hackable Run和一个可以禁用漏洞并独立检查任务成功的Ullackable Run进行评估. 并追踪整个训练过程的动态。
